  "prefLabel": "Lab 517.03 Waiver or Suspension of Rules by Presiding Officer",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Lab 517.03 Waiver or Suspension of Rules by Presiding Officer. The presiding officer, upon the motion of any party or intervenor, or on his or her own initiative, shall suspend or waive any requirement or limitation imposed by this chapter when the suspension or waiver:\n\n(a) Appears to be lawful; and\n\n(b) Is more likely to promote the just, accurate and efficient resolution of the pending dispute than would adherence to the particular requirement or procedure.\n\nSource. #9287, eff 10-1-08; ss by #10038, eff 12-1-11; ss by #11067, eff 4-1-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/lab500.html"
